--TEST--
In a `directory` block, a folder name outside the directory and a refused flag throw `RuntimeError`, a folder or a UID that does not exist throws `IOError`, and a change without `fs.write` for the directory throws before any file changes — `rule:core-classes/imap`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: Core\Imap::open, Core\Imap\Mailbox::folders, Core\Imap\Mailbox::folder, Core\Imap\Folder::uidValidity, Core\Imap\Folder::search, Core\Imap\Folder::fetch, Core\Imap\Folder::move, Core\Imap\Folder::markSeen, Core\Imap\Folder::markUnseen, Core\Imap\Folder::flag, Core\Imap\Folder::unflag, Core\Imap\Folder::delete
// Each step below tries something a mailbox does not allow, and prints the error.
var $mailbox = Core\Imap::open("inbox");
echo Core\Str::join($mailbox->folders(), ", "), "\n";

// A folder name is one directory name, so `..` is not allowed.
try {
    $mailbox->folder("../secrets");
} catch (RuntimeError $error) {
    echo $error->message, "\n";
}

// The folder `Spam` does not exist.
try {
    $mailbox->folder("Spam");
} catch (IOError $missing) {
    echo "IOError: no folder Spam\n";
}

var $inbox = $mailbox->folder("INBOX");
echo "validity ", $inbox->uidValidity(), "\n";

// A UID is 1 or more.
try {
    $inbox->fetch(0);
} catch (RuntimeError $error) {
    echo $error->message, "\n";
}

// `limit` is 1 or more.
try {
    $inbox->search({ limit: 0 });
} catch (RuntimeError $error) {
    echo $error->message, "\n";
}

// Only `delete` may set `\Deleted`, and a keyword has no space.
try {
    $inbox->flag(1, "\\Deleted");
} catch (RuntimeError $error) {
    echo $error->message, "\n";
}
try {
    $inbox->unflag(1, "two words");
} catch (RuntimeError $error) {
    echo $error->message, "\n";
}

// No message has the UID 9.
try {
    $inbox->markSeen(9);
} catch (IOError $missing) {
    echo $missing->message, "\n";
}
try {
    $inbox->markUnseen(9);
} catch (IOError $missing) {
    echo $missing->message, "\n";
}
try {
    $inbox->delete(9);
} catch (IOError $missing) {
    echo $missing->message, "\n";
}

// The target folder `Spam` does not exist, so message 1 stays in `INBOX`.
try {
    $inbox->move(1, "Spam");
} catch (IOError $missing) {
    echo "IOError: no folder Spam\n";
}
echo "INBOX has ", Core\Arr::count($inbox->search()), " message\n";

// The block `shared` may be read but not changed, because `fs.write` does not list its directory.
var $shared = Core\Imap::open("shared")->folder("INBOX");
echo "shared has ", Core\Arr::count($shared->search()), " message\n";
try {
    $shared->delete(1);
} catch (RuntimeError $error) {
    echo "RuntimeError: shared is read-only\n";
}
echo "shared has ", Core\Arr::count($shared->search()), " message\n";
--FILE mailbox/INBOX/1.eml--
From: Ada <ada@example.com>
Subject: Hello

Hello.
--FILE shared/INBOX/1.eml--
From: Bo <bo@example.org>
Subject: Hello

Hello.
--FILE nvs.toml--
[imap.inbox]
directory = "mailbox"

[imap.shared]
directory = "shared"

[capabilities.imap]
connect = ["inbox", "shared"]

[capabilities.fs]
read = ["mailbox", "shared"]
write = ["mailbox"]
--EXPECT--
INBOX
Core\Imap\Mailbox::folder: `../secrets` is not a folder of `[imap.inbox]`. A folder of a directory block is one directory name, without `/`, `\`, `:` or `..`.
IOError: no folder Spam
validity 1
Core\Imap\Folder::fetch: `$uid` is 0, and a UID is 1 to 4294967295
Core\Imap\Folder::search: `limit` is 0, and it must be 1 or more
Core\Imap\Folder::flag: `\Deleted` cannot be set as a flag. To delete a message, call `delete`.
Core\Imap\Folder::unflag: `two words` cannot be set as a flag. A keyword has no space and none of the characters `(){%*"\]`.
Core\Imap\Folder::markSeen: the folder has no message with the UID 9
Core\Imap\Folder::markUnseen: the folder has no message with the UID 9
Core\Imap\Folder::delete: the folder has no message with the UID 9
IOError: no folder Spam
INBOX has 1 message
shared has 1 message
RuntimeError: shared is read-only
shared has 1 message
